Florida's governor and maybe

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.579
2024 presidential candidate Ron

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.899
DeSantis thinks so.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.969
We're not just going to sit idly by

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.679
if you're trying to circumscribe

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.719
people's freedoms and that's true

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.609
if it's government, it's also true

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:36.899
of it's big business.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.669
He's quickly becoming a favorite of

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.349
a conservative movement, seeking to

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.359
jettison the libertarian idea that

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.889
government shouldn't meddle in the

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.509
affairs of private business.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:47.369
But I think the lesson for people on

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.779
the right is I think there was a

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.059
generation of people that

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.889
kind of the muscle memory

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.199
was just if it's private, just defer

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:55.679
to it.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.239
Earlier this year, DeSantis and

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.129
Republicans in the state legislature

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.929
retaliated against Disney for

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.789
opposing a Florida law prohibiting

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.289
the discussion of sexuality and

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.179
gender identity in K through

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.769
third grade classrooms.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.659
Disney should not run its own

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:10.660
government.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.379
Now, DeSantis, who declined

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.029
our interview request, has signed

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.949
the Individual Rights Act,

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.809
formerly known as the Stop

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:19.799
Work Act.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.479
I think what you see now with the

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.269
rise of this woke ideology

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.939
is an attempt to really delegitimize

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:27.899
our history.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.209
A U.S. district court judge struck

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:31.949
down the first part of the law on

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.419
First Amendment grounds.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.189
It prohibited private companies from

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.049
holding any mandatory training that

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.209
espouses, promotes advances

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.369
inculcates or compels employees

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.979
to believe eight concepts.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.169
Those are that members of one race,

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.419
color, sex or national origin

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.249
are morally superior to members of

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.959
another race, color or sex.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.489
That your inherent characteristics

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.319
make you inherently racist, sexist

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.459
or oppressive.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.139
That these characteristics determine

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.299
one's moral status as privileged

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.189
or oppressed, or mean that

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.169
you bear personal responsibility

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.849
for past injustices.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.159
The concepts like merit, excellence,

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.019
hard work, fairness, neutrality,

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.759
objectivity and racial

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.709
colorblindness are racists.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:15.269
Or that trying to be colorblind and

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.249
treat people without regard to race

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:18.509
is wrong.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.309
Here's one example of a diversity,

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.409
equity and inclusion presentation

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.879
from one of the plaintiffs in the

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:24.749
lawsuit.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.849
Oftentimes, it's very

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.739
hard for us to distinguish

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.289
white supremacy from things like

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.159
these are just U.S.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.049
cultural norms, you know, a focus

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.419
on individualism over groups

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.429
or emphasizing written

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.199
word as a form of professional

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.369
communication.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.259
White supremacy culture is

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.179
why the posture of

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.489
white humility, from my perspective,

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.319
is so difficult for white

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.549
people to embody.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.259
Banning workplace trainings that

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.179
tell people that their race or sex

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.279
makes them morally culpable might

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.409
sound pretty reasonable,

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.389
but opponents say such laws

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.189
set a dangerous precedent.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.079
As you go through the concepts

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.969
the state worded in a way

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.639
that makes it seem terrible.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.379
Jerry Edwards is a staff attorney

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.759
with the American Civil Liberties

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.889
Union of Florida, who is challenging

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.269
a separate part of the law that

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.249
applies to universities.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.199
He calls the bill a wolf

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.309
in sheep's clothing.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:22.259
Because anytime a government bans

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.209
broad categories of speech,

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.489
it gives politicians the ability

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.799
to define terms of acceptable

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.269
discourse.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:31.169
It's problematic.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.209
And we can't allow the state can't

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.979
give the state this power to

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.449
regulate speech in a sort of way.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.449
The left also craves state

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.979
power to impose its cultural

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.209
preferences.

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:44.099
Nation writer Jeet Heer tweeted

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.169
recently that we should use

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:48.029
state power for good,

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:50.039
like civil rights and defending

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.619
the LGBTQ community.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.749
The only objection to DeSantis

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.879
is that he wants to use state power

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.919
to push big business to do bad

00:03:58.920 --> 00:03:59.879
things.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.889
Of course, from the perspective of

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.809
DeSantis and his allies,

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.849
the Individual Rights Act is

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:07.529
a civil rights law to force

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.689
businesses to do what they think

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.789
is good for Americans.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.709
By taking identity politics out

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.209
of the workplace.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.338
The more power politicians have

00:04:17.339 --> 00:04:19.259
to determine which type of speech

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.359
is good and therefore legal

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.249
and which is bad and therefore

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:25.499
illegal, the more the sphere

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.569
of acceptable discourse is likely

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.699
to shrink as both sides

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.649
of the political spectrum hem

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.259
in those boundaries to promote

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:36.119
their subjective notions

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.159
of the common good.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.409
The state should not be

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.179
banning ideas, particularly on

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.529
college campuses.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.539
When you have such a blatant attempt

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:48.389
to control thought

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:49.919
and not only control thought, but

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.479
have the state control thought,

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.939
that's reminiscent of societies

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.789
and governments that we supposedly

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.019
fought wars against.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.989
The part of DeSantis's law that

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:01.939
hasn't been struck down pertains to

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.769
universities that receive state

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:04.789
funding.

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.679
It bans college professors from

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.329
promoting any of the eight forbidden

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:09.169
concepts.

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:11.299
LeRoy Pernell, a law professor

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.129
at Florida A&amp;M University,

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:14.959
or FAMU an historically Black

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.699
College, is a plaintiff in the

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.799
ACLU's case challenging that

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.179
part of the law.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.039
He's afraid that the law will outlaw

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:24.289
discussions of systemic racism,

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.149
which he says is part of FAMU's

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.919
institutional history.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:29.419
The state created the law school in

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:31.489
1949 to accommodate

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:33.619
two black law students who applied

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.179
to the racially segregated

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:37.159
University of Florida.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.139
In 1966 the state

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:40.999
forced it to cease admitting new

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.499
students. Until then Florida

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.359
Governor Jeb Bush signed a law

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.459
to reopen it in 2000.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.259
Purnell worries that if instructors

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:50.149
were to characterize that history

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:52.099
as systemically racist,

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.599
they'd run afoul of the law's

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.219
restrictions around teaching the

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:56.389
concept.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:58.279
I have no way of

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:00.229
knowing that my passion

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.239
for teaching students about

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:04.269
history, about change,

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:05.629
about their ability to bring about

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.879
change I have no way of knowing

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.889
that that isn't offensive

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:12.019
to these subjective

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:13.819
judgers of what is endorsing what is

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:15.559
not endorsing, what is promoting

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.569
what is not in, not promoting.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:19.519
So I do now live with

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.409
the idea that at any moment

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.239
the state can come and take negative

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.339
action against me

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:26.629
because of my thought.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:28.369
Pernell also worries that the law

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.079
would prohibit him from teaching

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.909
material from his own book

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.709
about the racist roots of the

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:36.079
concept of colorblindness.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.909
It is impossible to

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.079
understand

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.469
the criminal procedure

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:44.569
and understand the issues

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.239
that arise in criminal procedure

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.699
without understanding that that

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:50.869
that the history has not been

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:52.219
colorblind.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.929
But the state has argued that it

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.969
does have a say over what's taught

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:58.429
at taxpayer subsidized schools.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.259
Teaching kids to hate

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:02.239
their country and to hate each

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:04.189
other is not worth one

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.139
red cent of taxpayer

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:06.649
money.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:07.669
What do you think about that,

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:09.529
specifically the fact that

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.809
the state has a say in this because

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:13.879
it involves public money and they

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:16.069
deem the teaching of this to be

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:18.109
harmful to the state's interest.

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:19.579
The state's done this before.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.139
I mean, this is not something new

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.479
back in the Red Scare era.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.459
They tried to crack down on

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:26.719
professors who they thought were

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.909
communists or communists

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:30.829
adjacent. And the state has

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.779
no business doing that of regulating

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:34.489
the marketplace of ideas.

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:35.989
In that way, there isn't a

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:37.729
compelling interest in the state

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:39.979
saying which ideas are acceptable

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:41.719
and which ideas aren't.

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:43.909
That is viewpoint discrimination.

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.199
Diversity is good for business in

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:46.579
many ways.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.019
Companies with diverse leaders are

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:50.061
