The Stop Work Act creates

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.149
a whole set of pretty flimsy and

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:08.339
vague standards that make it

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:10.109
kind of impossible for an employer

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:12.029
to figure out how to proceed.

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:14.219
How much concern do you have about

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.109
retaliation for putting yourself

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:17.669
out there and being part of a

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.109
lawsuit like this?

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:21.089
As a as a business leader, I

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.129
strive to

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:24.509
do what's right for my business.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:26.369
I strive to take good care of my

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:27.729
customers and my employees.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.299
And so for me,

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.549
you know, standing up as

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:34.349
a plaintiff in this case was an easy

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:35.549
decision.

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:37.139
It's one that my team was behind.

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:38.140
And,

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.709
you know, I moved my business to

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:42.749
Florida in 2017 from

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.909
California because Florida

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.349
was known to be a business friendly

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:48.269
state, because it was a place

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:49.709
where a lot of investment dollars

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:50.849
were coming in and people were

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.709
moving, going to colleges,

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.929
getting tech degrees and

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:57.029
big names, people like Bill Gates

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:58.289
and Jeff Vinik have invested

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.789
billions of dollars in the Tampa Bay

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:02.249
area specifically to make it

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:04.529
a tech friendly place for innovative

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:05.399
businesses.

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:07.199
And so I don't imagine that the

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.239
state of Florida is wanting to,

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:12.809
you know, do anything to undermine

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.339
the the billions of dollars that

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.499
have flown into the state to promote

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:17.609
business.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.669
We believe in education,

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:22.559
not indoctrination.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.979
If people are

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:28.019
thinking of themselves in terms

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.759
of their racial identity, that

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:30.899
didn't begin with critical race

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:31.799
theory.

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:32.669
All right.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.979
That began in

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:36.689
the womb and that began and with

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:37.979
their families. And it began in

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:38.819
society.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:40.739
So this is nothing that's that

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:43.499
you know, this is not indoctrination

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:46.079
of ideas that that

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:47.939
that have roots and things that

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.409
didn't exist before.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:50.849
So that's that's just that's just

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:51.850
silly.

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:55.139
But the idea that that

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:58.799
somehow it is a negative

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.689
to understand that there are

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:01.950
racial differences,

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.389
that as a society,

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:07.649
different races, different

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:09.029
communities bring different things

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:10.019
to the table.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:12.299
You might disagree with Pernell.

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.189
I'm also not convinced that teaching

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:16.079
law students to celebrate racial

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:17.999
identity and differences is the best

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.979
use of classroom time.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:21.209
But it doesn't really matter what I

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:22.709
think. A lot professor should teach,

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:24.419
and it shouldn't much matter what a

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:26.519
governor thinks about that either.

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:28.199
The relevant question really is not

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:30.089
what goes on in the classroom, the

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:32.219
boardroom or the break room,

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:33.989
but who gets to decide?

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:35.909
Let's say that there was a blue

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:37.979
state that did kind of the opposite

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:39.869
of this, and they said, we're going

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:42.209
to ban a professor who

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:44.219
has a different viewpoint and

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:46.559
thinks critical race theory is wrong

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:48.599
and that we should be

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:50.699
talking about colorblindness

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.469
as a legitimate concept and things

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:53.279
like this.

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:54.839
Any time you put state and band

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.459
together. Danger.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:57.539
All right.

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.759
Why does the state ban

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:00.760
any thought?

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:04.529
If we are in a free society

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:06.359
that exists

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:08.639
and develops based on

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:10.769
free exchange of ideas?

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:12.899
The state can't really banish

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:13.859
ideas.

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:16.169
It can make people more hesitant

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:18.359
to speak openly and honestly through

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:19.499
punishment.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.299
Hampering real communication that

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.729
way and makes solving hard problems

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:24.989
even harder.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.879
And there are a lot of hard problems

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.409
left to solve.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.389
Some so-called woke ideas

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:32.549
are pernicious because reducing

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:34.469
every injustice to an identity

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:36.989
based formula flattens nuance,

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:38.879
cultivates grievances, and can

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.589
create tension where none existed

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:41.399
before.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.169
As borne out by studies that find

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:44.549
diversity, training quite often

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.859
makes people more prejudice.

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:48.659
The simplistic and counterproductive

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.519
approach only further clouds our

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:52.559
view of real solutions and

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.239
real progress.

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.129
But is the situation really so dire

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.899
as portrayed by political operatives

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.999
like Chris Rufo, who stood beside

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.159
DeSantis as he introduced the law

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.899
and who calls critical race theory

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:05.309
and similar teachings?

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:06.479
Neo Marxism.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:08.849
It's not a benign philosophy about

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:10.439
teaching racism.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:11.939
It's a radical philosophy that's

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.559
rooted in Marxism.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:15.479
Even some libertarians have come

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:17.459
to look at the issue as a fight

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.409
against communism.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:20.819
The Libertarian Party's official

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:23.129
account tweeted that soon

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.749
parents will be required to help

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.879
enforce the state's Marxist queer

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.889
theorist critical race agenda at

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:29.879
home.

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:31.319
Parents who fail to adequately

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:32.699
indoctrinate their kids will have

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.289
them taken away.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:35.819
And when you believe you're fighting

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:38.009
an existential domestic threat,

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.959
it can justify all sorts of very un

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:41.819
libertarian, authoritarian

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:42.839
behavior.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:44.819
The party account defended Joseph

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:46.739
McCarthy while approvingly

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.659
quoting an anti-woke academic,

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:50.849
saying It's time to deal

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:52.769
with American communists for

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:54.089
real.

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:56.099
Joseph McCarthy in the Senate and

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.419
the Committee for Un-American

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:59.299
Activities in the House went

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:01.039
way overboard in their hunt for

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.389
communist infiltrators in the

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:04.369
government, eventually targeting

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:06.619
actors, writers, poets, musicians,

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:07.819
teachers.

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:09.199
And we're not even talking about

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.789
Soviet spies within the government

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:12.289
here, which is what kicked off

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:13.729
McCarthy's crusade.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:15.109
We're talking about professors

00:15:15.110 --> 00:15:16.729
teaching what they believe college

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:18.769
students need to hear and employers

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:20.449
training their workers in ways they

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:21.799
think will help create a more

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:23.929
harmonious workplace and virtue

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:25.639
signal to their customers and

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:28.219
ultimately help their bottom line.

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:29.389
We're talking about a state

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:31.099
government regulating the free

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:32.749
exchange of ideas.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:33.799
That's a bigger threat to our

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.629
liberty and to American values

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:37.279
than so-called wokeness ever will

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:38.149
be.

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:39.979
But this isn't the way to

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:41.059
stop woke.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:42.409
Does that mean you just have to roll

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:43.519
over and take it?

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:44.929
After all, as conservatives will

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:46.369
point out, the Progressive Left has

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:48.169
no problem using civil rights law to

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:49.849
push its ideas into the workplace

00:15:49.850 --> 00:15:51.589
and onto the college campus.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:52.909
Why shouldn't the right pick up that

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:55.189
tool and use it for its own ends?

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:56.989
Well, because you're sharpening a

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:58.039
tool for your opponents to

00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.749
eventually turn against you.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.459
Instead, you could be blunting or

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:03.679
even dismantling it if existing

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:05.119
laws are part of the problem.

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:07.039
Limit or repeal the laws

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:09.199
also build, improve and support

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.639
alternative institutions.

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:12.919
Ones that reflect your values.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:14.569
Don't work for buy from companies

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:16.039
that you think disrespect you or

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:17.779
attend colleges that spend a lot of

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.939
time on little of value.

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:21.799
They'll get the message some already

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:22.800
have.

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:24.889
If you really think woke ideas

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:25.969
should be stopped.

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:28.609
Fine. But be wary of shortcuts.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.169
That's often how you miss important

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:32.029
details and badly hurt

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:33.109
yourself.

00:16:33.110 --> 00:16:34.939
The long, hard path is

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:36.349
the one more likely to bring

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:38.089
enduring change.

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:40.279
Criticize, resist,

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:41.280
and when need be, opt-out.

